                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/representation+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %li
                %a{:href => "#classification"} Classification
              %li
                %a{:href => "#from_supermultiplets_in_higher_dimensions"} From supermultiplets in higher dimensions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super-algebra"} super
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            %em adinkras
            (
            %a{:href => "#FauxGates04"}> Faux &amp; Gates 2004
            ) is a graphical tool for denoting those
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representations"} representations
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+multiplets"}> super multiplets
            ) of the
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            algebras in
            %em one
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/time"}> time
            ) dimension (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetric+quantum+mechanics"} supersymmetric quantum mechanics
            with
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/number+of+supersymmetries"} N supersymmetries
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            generators act, up to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivatives"} derivatives
            and prefactors, by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutation"} permutation
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfield"} superfield
            components. These are called
            %em adinkraic
            representations (
            %a{:href => "#Zhang13"}> Zhang 2013, p. 16
            ).
          %p
            While adinkraic representations are special among all representations of the 1-dimensional
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensional+reduction"} dimensional reduction
            of representations (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplets"}> supermultiplets
            ) of higher dimensional supersymmetry algebras down to 1d are of this form, at least for dimensional reduction from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N = \mathbf{4}
            (
            %a{:href => "#GGMPPRW09"}> GGMPPRW 2009, section 3
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GatesHubschStiffler14"} Gates, Hubsch &amp; Stiffler 2014
          %p
            The classification of adinkras, and hence of adinkraic representations, turns out to be controlled by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+codes"} linear codes
            (
            %a{:href => "#DoranFauxGatesHubschIgaLandweberMiller11"}> Doran, Faux, Gates et al. 2011
            ) and to be related to certain special
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
            via
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dessins+d%27enfants"} dessins d'enfants
            (
            %a{:href => "#DoranIgaLandweberMendez-Diez13"}> Doran, Iga, Landweber &amp; Mendez-Diez 13
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#DoranIgaKostiukMendes-Diez16"} Doran, Iga, Kostiuk &amp; Mendes-Diez 2016
          %h2#definition Definition
          %blockquote
            %p
              For general background, see at
              = succeed "." do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics+--+supersymmetry"} geometry of physics – supersymmetry
          %p
            For
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N \in \mathbb{N}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1 \vert N}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super Lie algebra
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            that is spanned by a single generator
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            in even (i.e., bosonic) degree and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            generators
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Q
                      %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi I
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I \in \{1, 2, \cdots, N\}
            in odd (i.e., fermionic) degree, whose only non-trivial components of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Lie+algebra"} super-
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+bracket"} Lie bracket
            are
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi I
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi J
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mn 2
                  %msub
                    %mi δ
                    %mrow
                      %mi I
                      %mi J
                  %mi P
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo =
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mrow
                    %mo {
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 2
                            %mi P
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mi I
                            %mo =
                            %mi J
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mtd
                            %mtext otherwise
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  [Q_I, Q_J]
                  \\,=\,
                  2 \delta_{I J} P
                  \\,=\,
                  \\left\{
                  \\array{
                  2 P &amp; \vert &amp; I = J
                  \\\
                  0 &amp; \vert &amp; \text{otherwise}
                  }
                  \\right.
          %p
            This is the 1-dimensional
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+translation+super+Lie+algebra"} super translation super Lie algebra
            = succeed "-extended" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Minkowski+spacetime"} super Minkowski spacetime
          %p
            Consider then super
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra+representations"} Lie algebra representations
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1 \vert N}
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
            of smooth
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfields"} superfields
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1 \vert N}
            (regarded as a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            acts as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derivative"} derivative
            operator on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+functions"} smooth functions
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^1
            in each component. If in addition the representation is such that in the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
            the odd generators
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_I
            send even/odd basis elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mi i
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi_i
            to single odd/even basis elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ψ
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi_j
            (as opposed to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+combinations"} linear combinations
            of them), hence if the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Q
                    %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Q_I
            act apart from degree-shift and possibly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiation"} differentiation
            by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/permutations"} permutations
            on the components of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/superfields"} superfields
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^{1\vert N}
            is called
            = succeed "." do
              %em adinkraic
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Zhang13"} Zhang 2013, p. 16
          %p
            The corresponding
            %em adinkra
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bipartite+graph"} bipartite graph
            which expresses these permutations:
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AdinkraRule.png", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              table grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#DoranIgaLandweberMendez-Diez13"} Doran, Iga, Landweber &amp; Mendez-Diez 2013, p. 7
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/1dAdinkraExample.png", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#IgaZhang15"} Iga &amp; Zhang 2015, p. 3
          %h2#classification Classification
          %p
            The topology of an adinkra graph together with its edge coloring in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ⋯
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{1,2, \cdots, N\}
            is called its
            = succeed "." do
              %em chromotopology
          %p
            The set of adinkra chromotopologies is equivalent to the set of colored
            = succeed "-cubs" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+codes"} linear codes
            (
            %a{:href => "#DoranFauxgatesHubschIgaLandweberMiller11"}> Doran, Faux, Gates, Hubsch, Iga, Landweber &amp; Miller 2011
            ).
          %p
            (A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+code"} linear code
            of length
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+subspace"} linear subspace
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\mathbb{F}_2)^N
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔽
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{F}_2
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+field"} prime field
            with two elements and it is
            %em doubly even
            if every element has weight a multiple of 4.)
          %p
            see
            %a{:href => "#Zhang13"} Zhang 2013, chapter 2
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AdinkrasFromCode.png", :width => "600"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              graphics grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#IgaZhang15"} Iga &amp; Zhang 2015, p. 4
          %h2#from_supermultiplets_in_higher_dimensions From supermultiplets in higher dimensions
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensional+reduction"} dimensional reduction
            of the smallest
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplets"} supermultiplets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mi N
                  %mo =
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 4, N = \mathbf{4}
            supersymmetry down to 1d yield adinkraic representations (
            %a{:href => "#GGMPPRW09"}> GGMPPRW 2009, section 3
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#GatesHubschStiffler14"} Gates, Hubsch &amp; Stiffler 2014
          %p Corresponding adinkras for the chiral scalar supermultiplet (CM), the vector multiplet (VM) and the tensor multiplet (TM) look as follows:
          %p
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AdinkrasFrom4d.png", :width => "450"}/
          %h2#references References
          %p For an introduction to adinkras, see the talk
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lutian+Zhao"}> Lutian Zhao
              ,
              %em What is an Adinkra?
              (2014) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "http://math.sjtu.edu.cn/conference/Bannai/2014/data/20141213B/slides.pdf"}> slides pdf
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            The concept of adinkras was introduced into
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry"} supersymmetry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation+theory"} representation theory
            in:
          %ul
            %li#FauxGates04
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Faux"}> Michael Faux
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adinkras: A Graphical Technology for Supersymmetric Representation Theory
              %strong 71
              (2005) 065002 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0408004"}> hep-th/0408004
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevD.71.065002"} doi:10.1103/PhysRevD.71.065002
          %p and further developed in the article
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Faux"} Michael Faux
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"} Tristan Hübsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
              = succeed "," do
                %em On Graph-Theoretic Identifications of Adinkras, Supersymmetry Representations and Superfields
              %strong 22
              , (2007) 869-930 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0512016"}> arXiv:math-ph/0512016
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X07035112"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X07035112
          %p and many more (“DFGHIL collaboration”). For instance the relation to Clifford supermodules is discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Faux"} Michael Faux
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"} Tristan Hübsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
              = succeed "," do
                %em Off-shell supersymmetry and filtered Clifford supermodules
              %strong 21
              (2018) 375–397 &amp;lbracl
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math-ph/0603012"}> arXiv:math-ph/0603012
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s10468-017-9718-8"} doi:10.1007/s10468-017-9718-8
          %p kinetic terms are discussed in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Faux"} Michael Faux
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"} Tristan Hübsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
              %em Adinkras and the Dynamics of Superspace Prepotentials
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0605269"}> arXiv:hep-th/0605269
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://inspirehep.net/literature/717895"} InSpire:717895
          %p
            The classification of adinkras in terms of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graphs"} graphs
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+codes"} linear codes
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#DoranFauxGatesHubschIgaLandweberMiller11
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Faux"} Michael Faux
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"} Tristan Hübsch
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
              = succeed "," do
                %em Codes and Supersymmetry in One Dimension
              %strong 15
              (2011) 1909-1970 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1108.4124"}> arXiv:1108.4124
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2011.v15.n6.a7"} doi;10.4310/ATMP.2011.v15.n6.a7
          %p and discussed in mathematical detail in
          %ul
            %li#Zhang11
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+X+Zhang"}> Yan X Zhang
                ,
                %em Adinkras for Mathematicians
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1111.6055"}> arXiv:1111.6055
                )
            %li#Zhang13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+X+Zhang"}> Yan X Zhang
                \:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The combinatorics of Adinkras
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Zhang-Adinkras.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimensional+reduction"} dimensional reduction
            of the standard
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermultiplets"} supermultiplets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 4, \mathcal{N} = 1
            supersymmetry to adinkraic representations of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo =
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒩
                  %mo =
                  %mn 4
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = 1, \mathcal{N}=4
            is due to
          %ul
            %li#GGMPPRW09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                , J. Gonzales, B. MacGregor, J. Parker, R. Polo-Sherk, V. G. J. Rodgers, L. Wassink,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4D
                    ,
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝒩
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 1
                    Supersymmetry Genomics (I)
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0902.3830"} arXiv:0902.3830
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1126-6708/2009/12/008"} doi:10.1088/1126-6708/2009/12/008
            %li#GatesHubschStiffler14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tristan+H%C3%BCbsch"} Tristan Hübsch
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adinkras and SUSY Holography
                %strong 29
                7 (2014) 1450041 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1208.5999"}> arXiv:1208.5999
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X14500419"} doi;10.1142/S0217751X14500419
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#IgaZhang15
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"}> Kevin Iga
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yan+Zhang"} Yan Zhang
              %em Structural Theory of 2-d Adinkras
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1508.00491"}> arXiv:1508.00491
              )
          %p
            Discussion for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo =
                    %mn 11
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D=11
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒩
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}=1
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"}> Jim Gates
              , Yangrui Hu, S.-N. Hazel Mak,
              %em
                Adinkra Foundation of Component Decomposition and the Scan for Superconformal Multiplets in 11D,
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝒩
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 1
                Superspace
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.08502"}> arXiv:2002.08502
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP09(2020)089"} doi:10.1007/JHEP09(2020)089
          %p
            The relation of adinkras to special
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Riemann+surfaces"} super Riemann surfaces
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dessins+d%27enfants"} dessins d'enfants
          %ul
            %li#DoranIgaLandweberMendez-Diez13
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Greg+Landweber"} Greg Landweber
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%A9ndez-Diez"} Stefan Méndez-Diez
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometrization of
                    = succeed "-Extended" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                %strong 19
                5 (2015) 1043-1113 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1311.3736"}> arXiv:1311.3736
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://dx.doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2015.v19.n5.a4"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2015.v19.n5.a4
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.charlesdoran.net/uploads/6/7/5/1/6751141/22_geometrization_of_n_extended_1_dimensional_supersymmetry_algebras_i_2015.pdf"} pdf
            %li#DoranIgaKostiukMendes-Diez16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Doran"}> Charles Doran
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"} Kevin Iga
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stefan+M%C3%A9ndez-Diez"} Stefan Méndez-Diez
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    Geometrization of
                    = succeed "-Extended" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi 𝒩
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}
                %strong 22
                3 (2018) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1610.09983"}> arXiv:1610.09983
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Further developments:
          %ul
            %li#CalkinsGatesGatesStiffler15
              %p
                Mathew Calkins, D. E. A. Gates,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
                Jr., Kory Stiffler,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Adinkras, 0-branes, Holoraumy and the SUSY QFT/QM Correspondence
                %strong 30
                11 (2015) 1550050 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.00101"}> arXiv:1501.00101
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217751X15500505"} doi:10.1142/S0217751X15500505
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."}> S. James Gates Jr.
                , Isaiah B. Hilsenrath, Saul Hilsenrath:
                %em
                  Modern Tensor-Spinor Symbolic Algebra Algorithms and Computing Non-Closure Geometry &amp; Holoraumy in
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 11
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 11D
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 1
                  Supergravity
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.00614"}> arXiv:2212.00614
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."}> S. James Gates Jr.
                , Yangrui Hu:
                %em
                  Adynkra Genomes, Adynkrafields, and the 4D,
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 1
                  Supergravity Superfield Prepotential
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2407.09334"}> arXiv:2407.09334
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spectral+triples"} spectral triples
            is in
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Matilde+Marcolli"}> Matilde Marcolli
              , Nick Zolman,
              %em Adinkras, Dessins, Origami, and Supersymmetry Spectral Triples
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1606.04463"}> arXiv:1606.04463
              )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wes Caldwell, Alejandro Diaz, Isaac Friend,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Gates"} Jim Gates
                %em
                  On the Four Dimensional Holoraumy of the
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mn 4
                          %mi D
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4D
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N} = 1
                  Complex Linear Supermultiplet
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1702.05453"}> arXiv:1702.05453
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kevin+Iga"}> Kevin Iga
                ,
                %em Adinkras: Graphs of Clifford Algebra Representations, Supersymmetry, and Codes
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2110.01665"}> arXiv:2110.01665
                )
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adinkra_symbols_(physics)"} Adinkra symbols (physics)
          %p
            In relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+spinors"} pure spinors
          %ul
            %li
              Richard Eager,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simone+Noja"} Simone Noja
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Johannes+Walcher"} Johannes Walcher
              %em Adinkras and Pure Spinors
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2404.07167"}> arXiv:2404.07167
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p
            Relation to
            = succeed ":" do
              %span.newWikiWord
                cellular automata
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/cellular+automata"} ?
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."}> S. James Gates Jr.
              , Youngik (Tom) Lee:
              %em A Précis: Minimal Four Color Holoraumy and Wolfram’s “New Kind of Science” Paradigm
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2408.09342"}> arXiv:2408.09342
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Jeth Arunseangroj, Jude Bedessem,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S.+James+Gates+Jr."} S. James Gates Jr.
              %em Adinkras &amp; Genomics in Sixteen Color Systems (I)
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.13797"}> arXiv:2503.13797
              \&amp;rbrack;
        .revisedby
